    <string name="epilogue_crown_restored">The council rises as one and the gold seal falls. By morning the gallery is swept, the masks are burned, and the court remembers nothing but a quiet, certain voice.</string>
    <string name="epilogue_quiet_coronation">The crown changes hands without music. Half the chamber still doubts, and the doubt will outlive the candles, but the right heir keeps the signet.</string>
    <string name="epilogue_jester_laughs">Somewhere behind the drapes a bell of small brass bells shakes. You named a liar and the liar bowed. The true heir says nothing at all.</string>
    <string name="epilogue_court_in_shadow">No contradiction was ever sealed. The council votes in the dark, the wrong hand takes the signet, and the gallery stays silent for a very long year.</string>

